>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_ersatz`

``` hol4
Refute.register_ersatz :
  {original : {Thy : string, Name : string},
   replacement : {Thy : string, Name : string}} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces one model-finder constant substitution.

When model-finder preprocessing meets the `original` constant, it
instantiates `replacement` to the occurrence's type and encodes that
instead.  A later row with the same original key replaces an earlier
session-local row and shadows a built-in one.  An active fraction
registration takes precedence: a colliding row is retained but takes
effect only once that registration is replaced or removed.

Neither name is resolved, and no types are checked, at registration
time; an absent constant or a replacement that cannot be retyped is
reported when preprocessing uses the row.  No HOL constant or theorem is
created.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model-finder preprocessing is described in
\ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
